The streaming XLSX implementation was tested in the same package invocations as
the forwarding changes. Raw output is shared to avoid duplicating logs:

Unit: forwarding-unit.log; selector includes TestUsageExport*.
Race: forwarding-race.log; selector includes TestUsageExport*.
Three benchmark rounds: forwarding-bench.log, BenchmarkUsageExportXLSX-4.
Exact commands and environment: forwarding-commands.log.

XLSX coverage: valid ZIP/XML parts, 37 columns, English/Chinese headings, original
RFC3339Nano times, reasoning labels and requested/effective effort fallback,
six/eight-decimal costs and fixed safety fee isolation, four-significant-digit
multipliers, literal formula-like strings, XML/SpreadsheetML escaping, UTF-16
cell limits, writer errors, close idempotency and writes after close.

Each benchmark operation streams 1,000 rows using one 64 KiB buffered worksheet
writer, without a shared string table or retained worksheet rows. Reported B/op
is cumulative allocation, not retained heap or process RSS.
